# Coding standards

## General

- **Minimize scope** — only change what the task requires
- **Match existing style** — naming, imports, error handling, folder layout
- **No over-engineering** — no extra abstractions for one-off use
- **Self-explanatory code** — comments only for non-obvious business rules

## Monorepo

- Put cross-platform enums/utils in `packages/shared/src/`
- Export new shared symbols from `packages/shared/src/index.js`
- Mobile and API both depend on `@localite/shared`

## API (`apps/api`)

- ES modules (`import`/`export`); `.js` extensions on relative imports
- Routes: thin — validate input, call service, return JSON
- Business logic in `services/`; DB access via Sequelize models
- Use `logger` from `src/logging/logger.js` — not `console.log`
- Errors: throw with `statusCode` or use `OrderStateError`; `errorHandler` middleware formats response
- Auth: `authenticate`, `requireRole`, `requireOnboarded`, `requireShopAccess` from `middleware/auth.js`
- Never log secrets, tokens, or full OTP values

## Mobile (`apps/mobile`)

- Screens under `src/screens/{role}/`
- API calls only through `src/services/api.js`
- Log errors with `src/logging/logger.js`
- Use `@localite/shared` for order status, enums, catalog helpers
- Secure tokens via `expo-secure-store` (handled in `api.js`)

## Database

- Schema changes: add migration in appropriate `*SchemaMigration.js` service
- Update `docs/architecture.md` and `docs/app.sql` when schema changes

## Security

- No secrets in code or committed files
- Rate-limit sensitive endpoints (auth, logs)
- Validate and sanitize user input on the API

